1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[Gon] He’s so far beyond me.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
But he’s not so far out of reach
I can’t catch up someday.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
I need more training in Nen.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I’ve gotta find a power
that’s as strong as Hisoka’s!

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
[theme song playing]

6
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
[birds squawking]

7
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,000
[Gon] Aunt Mito!

8
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Aunt Mito!

9
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Aunt Mito, hey!

10
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Gon.

11
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Gon!

12
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Aunt Mito!

13
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
[Gon laughs]

14
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
I’m finally home!

15
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Welcome back.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
And you must be Killua.

17
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
What?

18
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
GING X AND X GON

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[Mito] My goodness,

20
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I wish you’d let me know
you were coming home.

21
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
I didn’t have time to prepare!

22
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
It’s fine. No big deal.

23
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Maybe not to you!

24
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
But your friend just came all this way…

25
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
[Killua] Oh, don’t worry about me!

26
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
[Mito]
Honestly, you should’ve called at least!

27
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
I’ve been worried sick!

28
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[Mito] Are you listening?

29
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[muffled laughter]

30
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Mito] Oh, right.

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
You two go and take your baths
while I finish supper.

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
And put out all of your dirty clothes.

33
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
I’ll do laundry.

34
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
-[Gon] Okay, later.
-Right now!

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You’ve got ten seconds!

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
-One. Two. Three.
-[Gon] Ooh!

37
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
-Is she always like this?
-[Mito] Four.

38
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
-Five.
-Pretty much.

39
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
-[Mito] Six. Seven.
-Come on. Hurry up!

40
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Mito] Eight. Nine. Ten.

41
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Yeah… Now this is what I call living!

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
[Mito] Okay, let's eat.

43
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[Killua] Wow! It looks delicious!

44
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
What’s going on?

45
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
We’re offering our gratitude.

46
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
-‘Kay, what does that mean?
-Well? Let’s dig in!

47
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Please, help yourself
to whatever you like!

48
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
[Killua] Thanks!

49
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
-[Gon] Oh yeah… Aunt Mito.
-Hmm?

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Look!

51
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
This is a Hunter License.

52
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Wow…

53
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
It looks pretty ordinary.

54
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:22,000
There.

55
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
[Gon yelps]
Come on! What do you think you’re doing?!

56
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
[Mito laughs] I’m kidding!

57
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
You know I wouldn’t do that.

58
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[Gon] Well… I just hope it still works.

59
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Aunt Mito!

60
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
I’m gonna go show Killua
around the island! ‘Kay?

61
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
But won’t that take a while?

62
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Want me to pack lunch?

63
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
[Gon] It’s okay!

64
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
We’ll find something to eat in the forest!

65
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[Gon] Whoa!

66
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
[both laughing]

67
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
-[Killua straining]
-[both laughing]

68
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Where are they? It’s getting late.

69
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
It’s been a little while
since he was last home.

70
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
And it’s the first time
he brought a friend with him.

71
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
They’ll be back pretty late.

72
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,000
I’m sure they’re fine.

73
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Yes, you’re probably right.

74
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Maybe I should take some food out to them.

75
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[crickets chirping]

76
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
-[Killua] Hey, Gon…
-Hm?

77
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
So, uh… What are you gonna do now?

78
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
[Gon] Well, I think I’m gonna rest up here
for a little bit

79
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
while I gather all the information
that I’m gonna need.

80
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
For when I finally go to Yorknew City
to find my dad.

81
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
[Killua] Oh.

82
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
I gotcha.

83
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
What do you think I should do?

84
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
You should stay here, too!

85
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Then go to Yorknew City with me!

86
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
I know. I am coming with you.

87
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
But that isn’t what I meant.

88
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
I was just thinking I admire you.

89
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
There’s nothing I wanna do.

90
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
You’ve got your thing.

91
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
I don’t have anything.

92
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
There are plenty of things
I don’t wanna do, though.

93
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Like stay in that house,

94
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
or take over the family business.

95
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
I guess I’m a little bit... jealous.

96
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
-[Gon] Killua.
-Huh?

97
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
It’s fun.

98
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Hanging out with you, I mean.

99
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Hey… Where did that come from?

100
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Whale Island’s an outpost.

101
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
It’s where fishermen stay
when they’re at sea a long time.

102
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Not a lot of people who live here
are natives.

103
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,000
There is a girl around my age

104
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
but I just never got to know her
very well.

105
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
So, you’re kinda my first friend.

106
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
My same age and everything!

107
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Yeah, I know what you mean.

108
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Being stuck in that house all day…

109
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
and spending all my time
learning how to kill people.

110
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
You were my first real friend.

111
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
When we’re together, you have fun, right?

112
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Huh?

113
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I guess so, yeah.

114
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
I do too, so I think
we should stick together!

115
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Let’s travel around
and see the whole world!

116
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Just you and me!

117
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
You don’t know how embarrassing
you’re being right now, huh?

118
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[Gon chuckles sheepishly]

119
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I’ll go look for my dad…

120
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
and you can look for something
you really want to do.

121
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
It’s gonna be so fun!

122
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
You’re right.

123
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Doesn’t sound half bad.

124
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Fine! I’ll look for something to do…

125
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
but in the meantime,
I’ll help you find your dad!

126
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Mhm.

127
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Oh...

128
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
I forgot.

129
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
You never told me what your mom does.

130
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[Gon] It’s hard to ask about my dad,

131
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
but asking about my mom’s even harder.

132
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
It’s just that since Aunt Mito
raised me all by herself…

133
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
it feels weird, you know?

134
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Like it’s wrong or something.

135
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Is that how it works?

136
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
[Gon] When I was little,

137
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Aunt Mito told me that both my parents
died in a traffic accident.

138
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
She thought if I learned my dad
was alive and a Hunter,

139
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
that I might end up just like he did, so…

140
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
She didn’t know how right she was, huh?

141
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
[Gon] When I found out about my dad…

142
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
I dunno, I guess

143
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
I kind of decided
that if he was still alive somewhere,

144
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
my mom must’ve been the one who died.

145
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
That’s pretty harsh. Seriously.

146
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Ever since then…

147
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I’ve thought of Aunt Mito as my mom.

148
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
The only one I’ve got.

149
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
So, there’s nothing for me to ask

150
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
and I don’t need to.

151
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
I see.

152
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Ah, man…

153
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
I wish I had a mom
that was as cool as your Aunt Mito.

154
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
She’s awesome!

155
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Even if she does nag a lot.

156
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,000
[Killua] That's nothing.

157
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,000
If I just say I want to go outside,
my mom immediately starts crying.

158
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
No kidding!

159
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
-She gets hysterical and everything.
-[both laughing]

160
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
[Killua] Just the other day…

161
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
-Hey, Gon…?
-Yeah?

162
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
How long will you two be staying here?

163
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Maybe about… a month?

164
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
And after that…

165
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
I’m thinking about going
to look for my dad.

166
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[sighs]

167
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
What’s that?

168
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
-It’s something Ging left with me.
-What?

169
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
He asked me to give this to you
when you became a Hunter.

170
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[Gon] So Dad left this for me?

171
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Mito] If you want…

172
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
I’ll tell you all I know about Ging.

173
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Well, Gon, Ging is my cousin.

174
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
My first memory of him
is actually of his back.

175
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
I ran after him everywhere he went.

176
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I think I was about three…

177
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Looking back on it now,

178
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
it feels like all I ever did
was try to keep up with him.

179
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
When he was just twelve years old,

180
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Ging left the island
and took the Hunter Exam,

181
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
same as you.

182
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Out of nowhere,
he just said he was leaving.

183
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
But when I asked him why,

184
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
all he said was…

185
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
“There’s something I want.”

186
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,000
But then, he never actually told me
what it was he wanted.

187
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
So, we argued.

188
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Rather... I was the only one
doing all the arguing.

189
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:52,000
But… I never got to see Ging again
before he packed up and left.

190
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[Great Grandmother]
Originally, you were told

191
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
your parents died
in a traffic accident, right?

192
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
That was actually
what happened to Mito’s parents.

193
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Oh...

194
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:08,000
[Great Grandmother] It happened
not long after Ging left the island.

195
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
After that,

196
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Ging’s dad went on a fishing trip

197
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
and then just mysteriously disappeared.

198
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
In the end,

199
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
I lost both of my sons
in a very short time.

200
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Yes.

201
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
All that happened after he went away.

202
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Ging eventually returned to the island
nearly ten years later.

203
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
When he did,

204
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
he was carrying you with him.

205
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
You were still just a little baby.

206
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
He just showed up,
completely out of the blue

207
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
and asked us to take care of you
for a while.

208
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
I asked him about your mother

209
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
but all he would say is
they were separated.

210
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
And right when I was about
to agree to take you,

211
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
all of a sudden, she started yelling:

212
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
“Are you crazy?!” just like that.

213
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
And I imagine everyone on the island
heard it.

214
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Grandma! You don’t need to tell 'em that!

215
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Now, as I was saying…

216
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
I knew we couldn’t rely on Ging
to raise you by himself.

217
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Anyway, we really don’t know
anything about your mother.

218
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Mito even yelled:

219
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
“Don’t you ever come back here!”

220
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
And... She was crying and everything.

221
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Please! Grandma!

222
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Where was I?

223
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Oh, yes.

224
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
That’s when Ging left this little box
with us.

225
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
This girl…

226
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,000
She tried to throw it away so many times…

227
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Well, I wouldn’t have had to,

228
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:40,000
if someone didn’t keep putting it back
right where it was every time!

229
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[Great Grandmother]
If you really wanted to get rid of it,

230
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
you wouldn’t have tossed it
in a trash can.

231
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
You’d have burned it
or buried it at least.

232
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[huffs]

233
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
[sighs] You understand?

234
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
And that’s pretty much it.

235
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
That’s every last thing
I know about Ging Freecss.

236
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[Gon] Ging.

237
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Ging, huh?

238
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
I mean...

239
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Is that…?

240
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Yeah! Yeah, that sounds better!

241
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Ging…

242
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Aunt Mito…

243
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Tell me more about him.

244
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
What was Ging like when he was little?

245
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Oh… sorry.

246
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Does it sound weird for me
to use his name?

247
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
It just felt more… natural, I guess.

248
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[sighs] No, that’s not it.

249
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
You want to hear what he was like
as a child?

250
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Yes!

251
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
So… did Ging have any other friends here?

252
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Like, his age?

253
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Not really.

254
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
The only kids around here
were myself and your father.

255
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Of course,

256
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I was always practically begging him
to go and play with me,

257
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,000
but when I did, he would just run off.

258
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:59,000
You’d follow him
and you’d get lost every time.

259
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Really?

260
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Thanks!
We can always count on you, Grandma!

261
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
You’d follow Ging
way up into the mountains

262
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
but then you wouldn’t return.

263
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:13,000
The whole village would panic
when Ging came back by himself.

264
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
And it happened many times.

265
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
But when we would all go off
into the mountains to search,

266
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Ging would always be
the first to find you,

267
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
without fail.

268
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
It didn’t matter where you were hiding.

269
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
It happened so often,

270
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
people started to wonder if it wasn’t
you and Ging’s idea of a little prank.

271
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:37,000
What? I would never do
something like that!

272
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[Great Grandmother] Well, maybe not…

273
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
but you were always hiding in places

274
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
none of us would ever think to look!

275
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
It was almost like
you didn’t want to be found.

276
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,000
I don’t remember that…

277
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Was that really how it was?

278
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Oh! That reminds me of another time
that Ging and I…

279
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
[snoring]

280
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
[Killua] Hmm…

281
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Okay. So...

282
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
this… is the box, huh?

283
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Hmm... Let's see...

284
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Uh… how do you open this thing?

285
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,000
I tried a whole buncha things
but it wouldn’t even budge.

286
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Mind if I use a bit of force?

287
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Go ahead.

288
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
All right…

289
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
[straining]

290
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
[panting]

291
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,000
No use.

292
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
This thing’s not normal!

293
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
I could twist open a regular steel box
no problem.

294
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
Mhmm.

295
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
And since we have no idea what’s inside,

296
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
we can’t exactly smash it, can we?

297
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Doesn’t make a sound…

298
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,000
[Gon] Hmm...

299
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:25,000
[Killua] Your dad told Aunt Mito
she was only supposed to give you this

300
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
after you became a Hunter, right?

301
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,000
[Gon] Yeah, that’s what I heard.

302
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Not ‘til you had become a Hunter… huh…

303
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Whoa…

304
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Wait a sec…

305
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
I got it!

306
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Gon…

307
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
There’s still one thing
we haven’t tried yet!

308
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Huh?

309
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
What’s something you have now

310
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
that you didn’t have
before you were a Hunter?

311
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Hey! You’re right!

312
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
My Hunter License!

313
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Except… there’s no opening for the card,

314
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
so that can’t be it.

315
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Killua] No, not that.

316
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
I meant Nen.

317
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
[clatter]

318
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
That’s what’s inside?

319
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
-Another box?
-Uh-huh.

320
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Regular steel plates.

321
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
No trace of adhesives.

322
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
What is it?

323
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[Killua] That design…

324
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Look familiar?

325
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,000
[Gon] Wait this is…

326
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
I know!

327
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
This looks just like the pattern
on the promise thread

328
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Mister Wing gave me.

329
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
The promise thread

330
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
was designed to snap
if Nen was ever used,

331
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
wasn’t it?

332
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
I’ll bet you this pattern

333
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
holds a power similar to Nen.

334
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
And it looks like…

335
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
maybe the card goes in here.

336
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
-Hey! It worked!
-Bingo!

337
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
[Gon] A ring...

338
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
and a cassette tape...

339
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,000
And a memory card?

340
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Look.

341
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
That pattern’s
on the back of the ring, too.

342
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
You should be real careful
before you try putting it on.

343
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
‘Kay.

344
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,000
You think Ging would…

345
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
try to do something to me?

346
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,000
[Killua] Better safe than sorry.

347
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Well… We can start by listening
to the cassette tape.

348
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Guess so.

349
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Oh! Can you copy it first?

350
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Yeah, sure. But why?

351
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Better safe than sorry.

352
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[static crackling]

353
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
[Ging on a tape] Hey… Gon.

354
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
So, you became a Hunter too, huh?

355
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Anyway…

356
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
I have a question for you.

357
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Do you…

358
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
want to see me?

359
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
[narrator] It was the first time
Gon had ever heard his father’s voice.

360
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,000
And it felt to him like Ging
was reading his mind

361
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
and getting right to the point.

362
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[theme song playing]

363
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[Gon] Coming up:

364
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

365
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

366
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

367
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

368
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Today, we're introducing Aunt Mito!

369
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
She raised me,

370
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,000
so she’ll always be my mom
as far as I’m concerned.

371
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
I really wish I had a mom like Aunt Mito.

372
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
She’s the best!
But she does nag a whole lot.

373
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
[both giggle]

374
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Gon] Next time: “Reply x From x Dad”!

375
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Earthquakes, thunderstorms, fires, or Dad…

376
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua]
Which one of those scares you most?

377
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Aunt Mito.
